{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a613a360d41479ef90670d5dad5ce4ae7723e7bdd3db5a36bc9fac4bd75dd341","digest":{"component_or_area":"reconciler workflow / GHA runner","key_entities":["reconcile-bridge.yml","merge.ours.driver","init.py:508-511","merge=ours",".bridge_state/*","reconcile-bridge-canary.yml","rebar init","_merge_ours_unit","tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py"],"problem_keywords":["merge driver","git configuration","reconciliation workflow","merge=ours attribute"],"propositions":["merge.ours.driver is set per-clone in init.py but never committed, so reconcile-bridge.yml workflow does not inherit it on the runner","when merge.ours.driver is undefined, git silently falls back to 3-way text merge for .bridge_state/* files instead of the local-wins behaviour the design assumes","reconcile-bridge-canary.yml obtains merge.ours.driver via its rebar init call but reconcile-bridge.yml does not call rebar init after bare worktree add","undefined merge driver causes the reconverge path to lazily fault large blobs during merge operations when blob:none filtering is applied","reconcile-bridge.yml must set merge.ours.driver=true before any merge step to enable correct .bridge_state/* conflict resolution on the runner"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787887697984313001,"uuid":"595d4fb7-f8db-4ac9-a830-0083621a73da"}